 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? The two most common ways are having the groom's family pay for the whole thing, or splitting it 50 50. Ask his parents. A lot of couples don't want to weigh in until they' asked. Not rude at all, it' common. Ask them, and they might surprise you. Then split it or ask your family if they' be in. Most families can cover themselves, and it' fair. Good plan. Just make sure he asks them, not you.",
